          "summary": "This lesson develops students' ability to multiply 2-digit numbers by 2-digit numbers using multiple methods. Key vocabulary: ones, tens, hundreds and estimate/estimation. Students explore the concept in small groups using a partitioning. The teacher then models the method with a partitioning, addressing the common misconception that students disregard place value and multiply the digits instead of their values. Students finish with independent guided practice and a workbook task to consolidate the skill."
