          "summary": "This lesson develops students' ability to solve word problems involving multiple operations, identifying key information and representing information using bar model diagrams. Students explore the concept in small groups using a bar model. The teacher then models the method with number bonds, addressing the common misconception that students believe they need to multiply or divide, not both. Students finish with independent guided practice and a workbook task to consolidate the skill."
